# vehje-ir. shame

Known gaps in the shipped representation. Each is an honest deferral, not a
silent hole.

## Match pattern representation

The `Match` form stores its arm bodies as a `NodeList` and defers the pattern
representation. No shipping consumer matches yet, so the pattern node kinds (the
destructuring shapes a pattern binds) land with the first matching consumer
rather than being guessed at now. Until then a `Match` carries its scrutinee and
arm bodies but not the patterns that select them, which is enough for the
traversal and check integrity passes and not enough to evaluate a real match.

## Raw payload encoding

The `Raw` escape-hatch node carries a `FamilyId` and a `NodeList` placeholder
for its payload, but the payload encoding is family-interpreted and no shipping
family defines one yet. The concrete payload shape (how a family serialises its
own node kinds into the Core arena through the `Raw` seam) lands with the first
family that needs it, so today a `Raw` node names its family and holds a
node-list slot the family will later interpret, and the framework treats it as
opaque.
